  "query_preview": "..\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW:\n\nThe southwest flow will continue across the region today with an \nupper trough digging over the Pacific Northwest. As a wave lifts \nthrough the flow on today, afternoon showers over central Montana\nwill expand slowly eastward through the late afternoon and into \nnortheast Montana in the evening. Wind Gusts currently look to be \nthe main threat with 60+ mph showing HREF Max Wind Gusts. However \nthese gusts appear to moderate out into the evening hours around \nthe time they move into northeast Montana. SPC has a slight risk \nfor severe thunderstorms over north central Montana with a slight\nrisk for the remainder of northeast Montana.\n\nTemperatures will remain warm through the end of the week with \nthe continued southwest flow into Montana and ridge over the \nnorthern plains. \n\nEarly next week as the upper ridge tilts westward and the west\ncoast trough closes off, another round of showers and\nthunderstorms will be possible across the region. \n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\nMinor deviations from NBM were made to short term pops and winds.",
